    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0524" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.3715/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Counselor of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-11T16:00:00-04:00">June 11, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>343. Your 668, June 10, 4 p.m. Inform Cuban Embassy that in view of the
                    uncertainty of the situation resulting from recent incidents<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d471-f1"/> we regret that we cannot authorize any of our naval
                    vessels to visit Spanish ports until we can feel reasonably assured that such a
                    visit could be made without undue risk. It is possible therefore that it may be
                    some weeks before we are in a position to comply with the Embassy’s request.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
